ceo_bio":"Ms. Susan P. Kennedy | CEO & Chairman | Age 64 | Compensation: $412,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 31 people. Revenue per employee of $526K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $171K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Cadiz, Inc. is a micro-cap industrials business with a $269M market cap on $16M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +122% over the past three years and +49% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -29% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $27M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 4.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 32% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 32% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-6.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 166% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 213% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Cadiz Inc. Announces $21M Registered Direct Offering of 5 Million Shares at $4.20 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/cadiz-inc-announces-21m-registered-direct-offering-of-5-million-shares-at-420-each","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793306344.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cadiz Raises $21 Million in Registered Direct Offering","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/cadiz-raises-21-million-registered-121700000.html","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793276796.0,"origin":"